# Monitoring

| Area | Baseline signal | Interpretation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Pipeline quality | Lakeflow expectation metrics | Invalid rows warned, dropped or failed |
| Input drift | Maximum mean shift / training standard deviation | Breach above 3; not a statistical drift test |
| Prediction behavior | Row count and prediction mean | Distribution summary per model version |
| Performance | Accuracy or RMSE/MAE after outcome joins | Unavailable until real labels arrive |
| Operations | Job failure, model version, scoring timestamp | Operational health, separate from accuracy |

The monitoring job considers the last 24 hours, writes `monitoring.metrics`, and logs
standalone HTML dashboards plus JSON to MLflow. It fails when there are no predictions,
null features or a mean shift above the threshold. Configure job failure notification
recipients before enabling schedules. The default does not send any messages.
The local demo demonstrates delayed labels; the remote adapter currently reports only
unlabeled behavior. Add your governed outcome table and join keys before enabling
remote performance metrics. The bounded example is not a fleet-scale drift service.

## Databricks data profiling

As an explicit follow-up after DEV approval, open Catalog Explorer, the predictions
table, **Quality**, then configure **Data profiling**. Choose an Inference profile,
`predicted_at` as timestamp, `prediction` as prediction, and `model_version` as model ID.
Use regression for forecasting, classification for binary classification. Add an outcome
column only after labels exist. Select the project monitoring schema for metric tables.
Use a baseline table with matching feature columns and model IDs; the JSON mean baseline
used by this demo is not a Databricks profiling baseline table.

Databricks profiling creates profile/drift metric tables and a customizable dashboard.
Configure refresh scheduling, failure notifications, and metric alerts in the workspace.
It needs UC, Databricks SQL, SELECT plus USE CATALOG/SCHEMA and MANAGE privileges.
Time-series/inference profiles initially analyze the preceding 30 days. Materialized
view profiles do not support incremental processing. Verify availability and expense
for the chosen workspace before enabling it. No profiling service or AI/BI dashboard
has been created or claimed as workspace-tested by this template.

See [data profiling](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/data-quality-monitoring/data-profiling/)
and [profile configuration](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/data-quality-monitoring/data-profiling/create-monitor-ui).
